  "question": {
    "text": "In the given circuit, charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> capacitor changes as C is varied from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> as a function of &#39;C&#39; is given properly by: (figures are drawn schematically and are not to scale)<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/db2e041f-e59d-4042-b38e-775ebf809ef3-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 218px;\" />",
